 I know, I know. It's Tuesday! Here's what's up:

 Beginning today, Future of Defense will arrive twice weekly. I'll be handling the Tuesday edition. Thomas Novelly will handle the Thursday edition. I'm stickin' to my schtick; Thomas has you covered on everything space . Questions? Complaints? Happy hour invites? Reply to this email. 🏭 Situational awareness: L3Harris Technologies secured a $250 million contract from Lockheed Martin to manufacture standard-range Guided Multiple Launch Rocket System propulsion. Work will be done in a new facility in Camden, Arkansas .

 What else: Countless new munitions, the Coast Guard's drone buy and South Korea's hypersonic glide vehicle success.

 Today's newsletter is 1,475 words, a 5.5-minute read. 

 
 
