 6. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 An MQ-9B long-range drone. Photo: U.S. Coast Guard

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🇺🇸 The U.S. Coast Guard is buying four General Atomics-made MQ-9B drones and related equipment for almost $248 million. The contract is through Customs and Border Protection.

 Why it matters: "This investment will give Coast Guard crews a longer-range view of our maritime domain, helping them detect threats earlier," Anthony Antognoli, assistant commandant and program executive officer for robotics and autonomous systems, said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: The Coast Guard's unmanned strategy is worth rereading. ✈️ The "script has flipped on power projection" and adversaries "no longer need comparable forces to hold American bases at risk," Hidden Level chief executive Jeff Cole told me in a recent conversation. "The most capable aircraft in the world simply cannot project power if they are vulnerable on the ground."

 Why it matters: Ukraine's Spiderweb operation was not a one-off. In fact, it's a source of inspiration for would-be attackers. 💭 My thought bubble: Tectonic has a great recent rundown on Hidden Level here . 📡 Israel Aerospace Industries unveiled Point@Air, an aerostat-based radar for long-range surveillance. It's based on the ELM-2083.

 Why it matters: Elevation has its benefits. "Seeing the battlespace is the starting point for every effective defense," IAI chief executive Guy Bar Lev said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: Aerostats ( blimps! ) deserve more love. 
 
